      "writtenOn": "2021-11-25T09:59:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would you rather have that explanation done as a comment in the header or as part of the commit log (or something else)?\n\nWould the following work:\nAs enabling the IEEE802154_6LOWPAN config changes the structure size/signature, the ieee802154_lowpan member needs to be moved out of struct net.\nSo a new struct ext_net is created to contain a struct net that matches the current kernel ABI definition + the required ieee802154_lowpan at its end.\nThat way, when allocating an ext_net struct, the resulting address can be used for struct net (as net is the first member) and ieee802154_lowpan address can be found using container_of().\nThis allows the kernel internal functions to keep using struct net as parameter for all functions (no ABI breakage) while enabling WPAN drivers.",
      "parentUuid": "76e1b6f7_77cb373f",
